from a \code{Female} column, coded \code{0} or \code{1}, as in \code{\link[=calc_clocks]{calc_clocks()}}. The age
distribution is also split by sex and by every column with two to eight
distinct values.

The \code{x} sections list each scoring problem from \code{\link[=summary.mc_result]{summary.mc_result()}} with
the clocks it applies to. They also give the age correlation of each clock
against the blood reference from \code{\link[=score_associations]{score_associations()}}. A bibliography of
the scored clocks from \code{\link[=cite_clocks]{cite_clocks()}} closes the report.

Warnings and messages raised while the report is built are listed at the
